-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1069: one event at 10. Taking it, `settler` finds that its
-- deadline of 2 has passed and records `x` = 1 at 2; `matcher` takes the act
-- and records `x` = 2 at 10. Nothing inside the RAND reads `x`. In time the
-- record is 1 then 2 (NORM-LOG-SPEC N20, ruled 2026-10-26: every deadline an
-- event reveals is settled before the event is matched).
-- Here the side that settles goes first, so the records are made in time order and the run answers, with `x` = 1 then 2.
IMPORT prelude
DECLARE Party IS ONE OF P
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF go, stay

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`matcher` MEANS
    PARTY P
    MAY go
    WITHIN 100
    HENCE COMMIT `x` IS 2 HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`settler` MEANS
    PARTY P
    MUST stay
    WITHIN 2
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST (COMMIT `x` IS 1 HENCE FULFILLED)

#TRACE `settler` RAND `matcher` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY P DOES go AT 10
